cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HELD in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "HELD: Held-out measurement for claimed AI and robot improvements"
abstract: >-
  HELD is a dependency-free tool that decides whether a claimed improvement in
  an AI system or a robot policy is real. It measures the candidate against the
  baseline on data that was never used to select the candidate, corrects the
  selection-split gain for the winner's curse, and reports the verdict, the
  uncertainty and the amount of held-out evidence the claim would require.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Balanov
    given-names: Anton
repository-code: "https://github.com/Balanov/held"
url: "https://balanov.pro/held/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-14"
keywords:
  - evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - self-improvement
  - robotics
  - statistics
  - agent evaluation
